Error [E0070]: this uses a retired arrow spelling
  --> tests/ui/cffi_abi_target_invalid.jet:4:35
    |
  4 |     #ABI(stdcall) fn ping(x: I32) => I32 = "ping"
    |                                   ^^
 Why: callables, arms, and lambdas use one arrow: `->`
 Fix: replace `:>` or `=>` with `->`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0070

Error [E0068]: this callable uses the retired result-arrow shape.
  --> tests/ui/cffi_abi_target_invalid.jet:4:35
    |
  4 |     #ABI(stdcall) fn ping(x: I32) => I32 = "ping"
    |                                   ^^
 Why: a return type sits after the parameter list, and `->` introduces the body; an effect ceiling follows the return type
 Fix: write `fn name(...) Type -> body`, or `fn name(...) Type -[Effects]> { … }`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0068

Error [E3213]: `stdcall` is not available on this target
  --> tests/ui/cffi_abi_target_invalid.jet:4:10
    |
  4 |     #ABI(stdcall) fn ping(x: I32) => I32 = "ping"
    |          ^^^^^^^
 Why: native calling conventions are restricted by operating system and architecture
 Fix: use the default C ABI or `system` for portable declarations
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E3213
